  "id": "COMPOUND:15394 - PROTEIN:1503",
  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside appears to be a common target of multiple compounds that ultimately influence G1/S-specific cyclin-D1 through a shared pathway involving Cytochrome c4. This suggests a potential mechanism where kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside may modulate the activity of Cytochrome c4, which in turn interacts with other compounds to regulate cyclin-D1. The presence of multiple independent pathways converging on cyclin-D1 through different intermediates highlights a possible role for Cytochrome c4 in the regulation of cyclin-D1, possibly through metabolic or signaling interactions. The integration of these pathways implies that the relationship between kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside and G1/S-specific cyclin-D1 may involve a complex network of molecular interactions, where the target of kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside is not directly the regulator of cyclin-D1 but rather a mediator in a broader regulatory cascade. This mechanism underscores the importance of Cytochrome c4 as a central node in the regulation of cyclin-D1, potentially linking kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside to the downstream effect via a metabolic or signaling pathway.",
